cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "omni-equations: a library of 67 verified equations as dependency-free Rust"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-16
abstract: "An equation library built by a clean-room factory from published definitions: modular and residue-number-system arithmetic, number-theoretic transforms, primality and factoring steps, VP9 inverse transforms and filters, Opus range decoding, fixed-point exp / ln / softmax. Each concept is one dependency-free Rust file with its definition (an s-expression), a property law, and recorded rows that a script re-checks from a clean clone. Pre-alpha. Published as defensive prior art."
authors:
  - family-names: "De Santiago"
    given-names: "Juan Carlos"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SovRing-Labs/omni-equations"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords: [equation library, residue number system, modular arithmetic, number theoretic transform, verified code, clean-room, Rust]
